Notes on Male Recode File

1.   There are 3 cases for which MV035 (number of wives) is
     missing.  For these cases, MV034 has one of the following
     conditions: 0 wives listed, 1 wife listed, or 3 wives listed.

2.   In the individual man's data, MV110 and MV111 are not
     applicable.  Please see SM113 and SM113B for information about
     exposure to radio and television.

3.   There are 2 cases in which MV135 (visitor/resident) is
     missing.

4.   The base for MV213 is men in union as well as those with a
     regular or occasional sexual partner.

5.   The base for MV867 is men who have had a birth since January
     1993.

Notes on couples (linking the male and female recode files)

In linking the couples that can be found in the women's and men's
recode files, there are some mismatches.  Only couples for which
there is consistency in reporting should be used for analysis.

1.   There are 48 cases in which the husband reported in V034 of
     the women's recode file is not in the men's recode file
     because he was not eligible.

2.   There are 44 cases in which the husband reported in V034 of
     the women's recode file is in the men's recode file, but he
     does not have a complete questionnaire.

3.   There are 10 cases in which the husband reported in V034 of
     the women's recode file is in the men's recode file, but he
     does not report the woman as his wife in his variable MV034.

4.   There are 131 cases in which the wife reported in MV034 of the
     men's recode file is not in the women's recode file because
     she was not eligible.

5.   There are 42 cases in which the wife reported in MV034 of the
     men's recode file is in the women's recode file, but she does
     not have a complete questionnaire.

6.   There are 16 cases in which the wife reported in MV034 of the
     men's recode file is in the women's recode file, but she does
     not report the man as her husband in her variable V034.


Inconsistencies in the Male Data File

1.   There are 3 cases in which the household office editor is not
     equal to the office editor recorded in the male individual
     data.

2.   There are 2 cases in which the respondent has been sterilized
     but provided a time for a desired future birth (MV602).

3.   There are 4 respondents who reported age at first marriage as
     less than 12 years.

4.   There are 26 cases in which MV630A (discussed family planning
     with partner) has a value even though the respondent is not
     currently in union.

5.   There was 1 case in the raw data file for which a response for
     MV853 and MV763 existed although the respondent had not had
     sex in the last year.  This response of no partners was
     corrected to NOTAPPL for both MV853 and MV763.

